DESCRIPTION Architecture style, the capabilities it favours, and the stressors it is built to survive
CATEGORY Architectural Capabilities
NAMESPACE TrStyleNS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall AS tr
DEFINE STYLE Total Recall AS Modular Monolith, local-first, one deployable per machine
DEFINE CAPABILITY Simplicity AS one Node process, Markdown files, no server to run
DEFINE CAPABILITY Cost AS zero runtime cost; optional embeddings run locally
DEFINE CAPABILITY Evolvability AS tools isolated behind one registry (TR-S5, TR-S11)

# Stressors and their residues. Machine-checked format ([TR-E1], stressor-residues.test.ts):
#   # S<n> <stressor description>: residue <TR-ID>[, <TR-ID>]*
# Every residue ID must exist as a tagged ASSERT somewhere in architecture/adl/.
# Residues are prioritised by the course's three tests — protects a core area,
# covers several stressors, probability × impact (REVIEW.md §8).
# S1 the host harness changes its hook API (Claude Code, Gemini CLI): residue TR-C5, TR-C1 (the per-host adapters are hooks/hooks.json and hooks.gemini.json)
# S2 the embedder or a native binding is missing: residue TR-R1, TR-R3
# S3 a teammate runs an older plugin version: residue TR-C1, TR-C6
# S4 the vault grows to tens of thousands of memories: residue TR-P1, TR-P2 (plus the untagged loadtest targets in capabilities.adl, to be tagged once they are automated)
# S5 a teammate pushes hostile org content: residue TR-D3, TR-D12
# S6 the embedding model, provider or cost changes: residue TR-R6, TR-R3, TR-R1
# S7 privacy rules gain new patterns: residue TR-D3, TR-D12
#
# Stressor × component × data-store incidence (what each stressor hits):
#   S1 → hooks/hooks.json, hooks.gemini.json (Lifecycle Hooks × host harness)
#   S2 → Vectors: embeddings.ts, vectorStore.ts (server quantum × vectors.db)
#   S3 → memory-file contract readers, org index.json (every reader × both vaults)
#   S4 → persistence: index.json, invertedIndex.json, .index-cache.txt (both vaults)
#   S5 → privacy-filter.ts, org index framing (org vault × org git remote)
#   S6 → Vectors + the vector-model-switch rebuild path (vectors.db)
#   S7 → privacy-filter pattern table, org injection framing (org vault × org git remote)
ASSERT(Each stressor above has at least one tagged assertion as its residue) # [TR-E1]
